{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Silo\/tutorials\/Silo\/BuildingAD6DiceRoller"},"metadata":{"categoryPathComponent":"Silo","title":"Rolling a D6","role":"project","category":"Silo"},"kind":"project","sections":[{"title":"Rolling a D6","estimatedTimeInMinutes":15,"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In this tutorial, you will build a D6 dice roller using Silo. The fetch is a single line — "},{"code":"Int.random(in: 1...6)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — so every concept you encounter is focused on Silo, with no boilerplate distractions.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"You will create a ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Silo\/documentation\/Silo\/DataSource","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" backed by a random number, drive a SwiftUI view from its reactive stream, wire up a Roll button, and configure the die to roll itself automatically while the view is on screen."}]}],"chapter":"Your First Data Source","kind":"hero"},{"kind":"tasks","tasks":[{"contentSection":[{"kind":"contentAndMedia","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Create a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DiceRoller"},{"type":"text","text":" service that holds a "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Silo\/documentation\/Silo\/DataSource"},{"type":"text","text":" for the last roll. Because the current roll may be absent before the die is first rolled, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int?"},{"type":"text","text":" is the appropriate type — "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":" means “not yet rolled.”"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"Optional","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is one of Silo’s built-in empty types, so no ","type":"text"},{"code":"emptyValue","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" closure is needed. The source starts as ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and updates to